# Tests for lot error behaviour.

# ** 1. no lots available with --lots errors (exits 1)
<
2026-02-01 sell
    assets:stocks    -5 AAPL {$50} @ $55
    assets:cash       $275
    revenues:gains

$ hledger -f- print --lots 2>/dev/null
>=1

# ** 2. Unclassified lotful commodity posting in asset account is a hard error with --lots.
# AAPL has lots: tag, assets:broker is an asset account, but the posting has no cost basis
# and no price, so classification fails. With --lots this is an error.
<
commodity AAPL  ; lots:

2026-01-15 mysterious
    assets:broker    10 AAPL
    income:mystery

$ hledger -f- bal assets --lots 2>&1
hledger: Error: -:4:
  | 2026-01-15 mysterious
4 |     assets:broker                                 10 AAPL
  |     income:mystery

AAPL is declared lotful (commodity lots: tag) but this posting was not classified as
acquire, dispose, or transfer. Lot state will not be updated.
Possible fixes: add a cost basis ({$X}), a price (@ $X),
or check the account type declaration.
>=1

# ** 3. Zero-amount lotful posting (eg a balance assertion) is not an error with --lots.
<
commodity AAPL  ; lots:

2026-01-15 check balance
    assets:broker    0 AAPL = 0 AAPL
    income:mystery

$ hledger -f- bal assets --lots 2>&1
--------------------
                   0  
>=0

# ** 4. Implicit zero-amount lotful posting (balance assignment inferring zero) is not an error with --lots.
<
commodity AAPL  ; lots:

2026-01-15 check balance
    assets:broker    = 0 AAPL
    income:mystery

$ hledger -f- bal assets --lots 2>&1
--------------------
                   0  
>=0

# ** 5. Non-lotful commodity in asset account does not error with --lots.
<
2026-01-15 normal
    assets:checking    $100
    income:salary

$ hledger -f- bal assets --lots 2>&1
                $100  assets:checking
--------------------
                $100  
>=0

# ** 6. Gain posting does not trigger unclassified error with --lots.
<
account revenue:gains  ; type:V

2026-01-15 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:cash

2026-02-01 sell
    assets:stocks    -5 AAPL {$50} @ $60
    assets:cash      $300
    revenue:gains

$ hledger -f- bal assets --lots 2>&1
               $-200  assets:cash
              5 AAPL  assets:stocks:{2026-01-15, $50}
--------------------
               $-200
              5 AAPL  
>=0

# ** 7. Bare acquire with no inferable cost errors with --lots.
<
commodity T  ; lots:

2026-01-17 buy
    assets:wj       -52 A
    assets:broker    2220 T  ; @ $0.01
    equity:conversion

$ hledger -f- bal assets --lots 2>&1
hledger: Error: -:5:
  | 2026-01-17 buy
  |     assets:wj                                    -52 A
5 |     assets:broker                               2220 T  ; @ $0.01
  |     equity:conversion

T is lotful but this acquire posting has no cost basis or price.
No lot will be created.

Postings were read as: unclassified, acquire, unclassified.
>=1

# ** 8. A leaf account name enclosed in `{...}` that is not a valid lot name
# errors at load time with the parse-failure message.
<
2026-01-01 literal brace account
    assets:project:{not a lot}    $1
    equity:opening               $-1

$ hledger -f - print
>2 /invalid lot name: not a lot/
>= 1

# ** 9. With --ignore-lots/-I, {...} leaf accounts are treated as ordinary subaccounts.
<
2026-01-01 literal brace account
    assets:project:{not a lot}    $1
    equity:opening               $-1

$ hledger -f- -I print
2026-01-01 literal brace account
    assets:project:{not a lot}                    $1
    equity:opening                               $-1

>=

# ** 10. `check lots` re-enables validation even when -I is used.
<
2026-01-01 literal brace account
    assets:project:{not a lot}    $1
    equity:opening               $-1

$ hledger -f- -I check lots
>2 /invalid lot name: not a lot/
>= 1

# ** 11. A lot subaccount name missing required parts (date and cost) also
# triggers the lot-subaccount error.
<
2026-01-01 only label
    assets:project:{"label only"}    $1
    equity:opening                  $-1

$ hledger -f - print
>2 /lot subaccount name must contain a date and cost/
>= 1

# ** 12. The unclassified-posting error shows the entry as written in the
# journal (balance assignments and elided amounts are not filled in), and
# mentions the problem posting's inferred amount, which is not visible in
# the excerpt (#2686).
<
commodity ABC ; lots:

2021-03-08 gift received
     revenues:gifts
     assets:broker1    = 2.3 ABC

$ hledger -f- bal assets --lots 2>&1
hledger: Error: -:5:
  | 2021-03-08 gift received
  |     revenues:gifts
5 |     assets:broker1                                   = 2.3 ABC

ABC is declared lotful (commodity lots: tag) but this posting (with inferred amount 2.3 ABC) was not classified as
acquire, dispose, or transfer. Lot state will not be updated.
Possible fixes: add a cost basis ({$X}), a price (@ $X),
or check the account type declaration.
>=1

# ** 13. An amountless gain posting is filled in with the calculated gain,
# also when the disposal is only recognisable after a balance assignment
# has been resolved (#2686): gain postings are set aside inside the balancer,
# once amounts are known.
<
commodity A  ; lots:
2026-01-15 buy
    assets:x1    1 A {$100}
    assets:cash

2026-02-17 transfer with priced fee
    assets:x1     = 0 A
    assets:x2      0.95 A
    expenses:fees  0.05 A @ $150
    income:gains

$ hledger -f- print -x --lots desc:transfer
2026-02-17 transfer with priced fee
    assets:x1:{2026-01-15, $100}                  -0.95 A {2026-01-15, $100}
    assets:x1:{2026-01-15, $100}                  -0.05 A {2026-01-15, $100} @ $150
    assets:x1                                      0 A                              =* 0 A
    assets:x2:{2026-01-15, $100}                   0.95 A {2026-01-15, $100}
    expenses:fees                                  0.05 A @ $150
    income:gains                                 $-2.50

>=

# ** 14. Referencing a lot that doesn't exist (here, a label the lot doesn't
# have) reports the non-matching selector and lists the account's available
# lots. #2689
<
commodity ABC ; lots:

2021-03-08 buy
     equity:open-close   -$10
     assets:broker1      2 ABC

2026-08-10 closing balances
    assets:broker1:{2021-03-08, "0001", $5}  -2 ABC
    equity:opening/closing balances

$ hledger -f- bal --lots 2>&1
hledger: Error: -:7:
7 | 2026-08-10 closing balances
  |     assets:broker1:{2021-03-08, "0001", $5}       -2 ABC {2021-03-08, "0001", $5}
  |     equity:opening/closing balances

no lots matching {2021-03-08, "0001", $5} for commodity ABC in account assets:broker1 on 2026-08-10
Available lots in this account:
  {2021-03-08, $5}  2
  Total: 2 ABC

Postings were read as: transfer-from, unclassified.
>=1

# ** 15. A transfer-like entry whose lotful-commodity quantities don't add
# up (eg a fee deducted in kind but recorded in cash) fails the balancedness
# check: no cost is inferred for the mismatched residual, which would mask
# the imbalance and surface as a confusing lot error instead. The error
# explains why no cost was inferred. #2692
<
commodity ABC ; lots:

2020-03-08 buy
     assets:cash        -$10
     assets:broker1      5 ABC

2020-04-05 transfer, quantities mismatched
     assets:broker1     -5 ABC
     assets:broker2      4.9 ABC
     expenses:fees       $1

$ hledger -f- bal --lots 2>&1
hledger: Error: -:7-10:
7 | 2020-04-05 transfer, quantities mismatched
  |     assets:broker1                                -5 ABC
  |     assets:broker2                                 4.9 ABC
  |     expenses:fees                                 $1

This multi-commodity transaction is unbalanced.
The real postings' sum should be 0 but is $1, -0.1 ABC
  -5 ABC  +  4.9 ABC  +  $1  =  $1, -0.1 ABC
Note, ABC is a lot-tracked commodity being transferred between accounts,
so no balancing conversion cost was inferred; its quantities are expected
to add up. If the difference is a fee, you can either
- record the fee expense in the lot-tracked commodity, with posting(s)
  adding up to the missing quantity
- or split the sending posting into a transfer part and fee part(s)
  matching the fee expense(s).
(With --ignore-lots, a balancing conversion cost is inferred instead.)
>=1

# ** 16. A balanced transfer-like entry where more of the lotful commodity is
# received than sent (eg sign errors or rounding-patched imported data) gets a
# direction-aware hint, since a fee can't explain that direction.
<
commodity ABC ; lots:

2020-03-08 buy
     assets:cash        -$10
     assets:broker1      5 ABC

2020-04-05 transfer, more received than sent
     assets:broker1     -4.9 ABC
     expenses:fees      -0.1 ABC
     assets:broker2      5 ABC

$ hledger -f- bal --lots 2>&1
hledger: Error: -:7:
7 | 2020-04-05 transfer, more received than sent
  |     assets:broker1                                -4.9 ABC
  |     expenses:fees                                 -0.1 ABC
  |     assets:broker2                                 5 ABC

Mismatched transfer quantities for lot-tracked commodity ABC: 4.9 transferred out but 5 received.
More was received than sent, which a fee can't explain;
check the entry for sign errors or rounding adjustments.

Postings were read as: transfer-from, unclassified, transfer-to.
>=1

# ** 17. Fee postings in the lot-tracked commodity which don't add up to the
# missing quantity exactly (eg here, a fee recorded alongside an in-kind
# rebate) are still an error, explaining the requirement.
<
commodity ABC ; lots:

2020-03-08 buy
     assets:cash        -$10
     assets:broker1      5 ABC

2020-04-05 transfer, fees don't match the missing quantity
     assets:broker1     -5 ABC
     assets:broker2      4.9 ABC
     expenses:fees       0.15 ABC
     revenues:rebate    -0.05 ABC

$ hledger -f- bal --lots 2>&1
hledger: Error: -:7:
7 | 2020-04-05 transfer, fees don't match the missing quantity
  |     assets:broker1                                -5 ABC
  |     assets:broker2                                 4.9 ABC
  |     expenses:fees                                  0.15 ABC
  |     revenues:rebate                               -0.05 ABC

Mismatched transfer quantities for lot-tracked commodity ABC: 5 transferred out but 4.9 received.
If the difference is a fee, you can either
- record the fee expense in the lot-tracked commodity, with posting(s)
  adding up to the missing quantity
- or split the sending posting into a transfer part and fee part(s)
  matching the fee expense(s).

Postings were read as: transfer-from, transfer-to, unclassified, unclassified.
>=1

# ** 18. A generic (unselected) outflow with insufficient lots reports just
# the needed and available quantities, without listing lots.
<
commodity ADA ; lots:

2026-01-01 reward
    assets:wallet    2 ADA @ $0.41
    revenues:staking

2026-01-02 reward
    assets:wallet    2 ADA @ $0.42
    revenues:staking

2026-01-03 reward
    assets:wallet    2 ADA @ $0.43
    revenues:staking

2026-01-04 reward
    assets:wallet    2 ADA @ $0.44
    revenues:staking

2026-01-05 reward
    assets:wallet    2 ADA @ $0.45
    revenues:staking

2026-01-06 reward
    assets:wallet    2 ADA @ $0.46
    revenues:staking

2026-01-07 reward
    assets:wallet    2 ADA @ $0.47
    revenues:staking

2026-01-08 reward
    assets:wallet    2 ADA @ $0.48
    revenues:staking

2026-01-09 reward
    assets:wallet    2 ADA @ $0.49
    revenues:staking

2026-01-10 reward
    assets:wallet    2 ADA @ $0.50
    revenues:staking

2026-01-11 reward
    assets:wallet    2 ADA @ $0.51
    revenues:staking

2026-01-12 reward
    assets:wallet    2 ADA @ $0.52
    revenues:staking

2026-02-01 sell too much
    assets:wallet   -60 ADA @ $0.50
    assets:cash     $30

$ hledger -f- check 2>&1
hledger: Error: -:51:
51 | 2026-02-01 sell too much
   |     assets:wallet                                -60 ADA @ $0.50
   |     assets:cash                                  $30

Insufficient lots for commodity ADA in account assets:wallet: need 60 but only 24 available

Postings were read as: dispose, unclassified.
>=1

