# ** 21. When a journal has both a lot error and a failing balance
# assertion, the lot error is reported first (assertion failures are
# deferred until the lot stages have run), even when the assertion
# comes earlier in the journal.
<
commodity ADA ; lots:

2026-01-01 buy
    assets:wallet    2 ADA @ $1
    assets:cash     -$2

2026-01-02 wrong assertion
    assets:cash      $0 = $-5

2026-01-03 sell too much
    assets:wallet   -5 ADA @ $1
    assets:cash      $5
$ hledger -f- check
>2 /Insufficient lots for commodity ADA/
>=1

# ** 22. With --ignore-lots (but not -I, which also ignores assertions),
# the same journal reports the assertion failure.
$ hledger -f- check --ignore-lots
>2 /Balance assertion failed in assets:cash/
>=1

# ** 23. An invalid date in a lot subaccount name is reported.
<
2026-01-01 buy
    assets:stocks:{2026-02-30, $50}    10 AAPL
    assets:checking
$ hledger -f- check
>2 /invalid date in lot name: 2026-02-30/
>=1

# ** 24. Two lots of a commodity with the same date and user-written label are an error.
<
2026-01-01 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {2026-01-01, "a", $50}
    assets:checking

2026-01-02 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {2026-01-01, "a", $60}
    assets:checking
$ hledger -f- check
>2 /lot id is not unique: commodity AAPL, date 2026-01-01, label "a"/
>=1

# ** 25. So is a user-written label that collides with an automatically generated one.
<
2026-01-01 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

2026-01-01 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {$60}
    assets:checking

2026-01-05 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {2026-01-01, "0001", $70}
    assets:checking
$ hledger -f- check
>2 /duplicate lot id: \{2026-01-01, "0001", \$70\} for commodity AAPL/
>=1

# ** 26. Transferring two lotful commodities with one amountless receiving posting
# is not supported; the error asks for separate postings.
<
commodity AAPL ; lots:
commodity MSFT ; lots:

2026-01-01 buy
    assets:a    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:a     5 MSFT {$60}
    assets:checking

2026-01-02 move
    assets:a   -10 AAPL
    assets:a    -5 MSFT
    assets:b
$ hledger -f- check
>2 /12 \|     assets:b
(.*
)*This transfer-to posting has amounts in several commodities \(10 AAPL, 5 MSFT\)\.
.*
please write these amounts on separate postings/
>=1

# ** 27. A new lot with a lot date but no cost, and no price to infer one from,
# is an error. Here the lot comes from equity, like an opening balance.
<
2026-01-01 gift
    assets:a    10 AAPL {2026-01-01}
    equity:x   -10 AAPL
$ hledger -f- check
>2 /2 \|     assets:a +10 AAPL \{2026-01-01\}
(.*
)*This posting creates a new AAPL lot, but its lot annotation \{2026-01-01\} has no cost,
.*
.*eg \{2026-01-01, \$50\}/
>=1

# ** 28. Under SPECID, a disposal must select a lot.
<
commodity AAPL ; lots: SPECID

2026-01-01 buy
    assets:a    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

2026-01-02 sell
    assets:a    -5 AAPL @ $60
    assets:checking   $300
$ hledger -f- check
>2 /SPECID requires a lot selector on dispose postings/
>=1

# ** 29. Under AVERAGE, lots with different cost commodities can't be averaged.
<
commodity AAPL ; lots: AVERAGE

2026-01-01 buy
    assets:a    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

2026-01-02 buy
    assets:a    10 AAPL {€40}
    assets:checking
$ hledger -f- check
>2 /cannot average lots with different cost commodities/
>=1

# ** 30. hledger's consolidated lot syntax can't be mixed with ledger-style [DATE] or (NOTE).
<
2026-01-01 buy
    assets:a    10 AAPL {2026-01-01, $50} [2026-01-01]
    assets:checking
$ hledger -f- check
>2 /hledger lot syntax \{\.\.\.\} cannot be combined with ledger-style \[DATE\] or \(NOTE\)/
>=1

# ** 31. Likewise when an amountless sending posting has a lotful commodity and cash.
<
commodity AAPL ; lots:

2026-01-01 buy
    assets:a    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

2026-01-02 move account contents back
    assets:b    10 AAPL
    assets:b    $5
    assets:a
$ hledger -f- check
>2 /This transfer-from posting has amounts in several commodities/
>=1
